{
  "$schema_note": "Each display entry describes how the visualizer should treat it. `resolution` is the framebuffer size [width, height] in pixels at native rotation. `mode` follows PIL modes: '1' (1-bit e-paper), 'L' (8-bit grayscale), 'RGB' (24-bit), 'P' (palette for multi-color e-paper). `palette` lists the actual colors renderable (used to quantize the framebuffer for realism). `shape` is 'rect' (default) or 'round' for circular LCDs — round displays mask the framebuffer to the inscribed circle so corners render black, matching the glass. `family` is 'epaper' | 'lcd' | 'oled' | 'char'. `char` marks an HD44780-style character LCD (e.g. LCD1602): it has no addressable framebuffer, so `char_grid` gives [columns, rows] and user code calls `display.text_lines([...])` to render the dot-matrix characters (plain `display.show(img)` still works too). `bezel` is the filename under backend/assets/bezels/. `screen_bbox` is the [x, y, w, h] rectangle inside the bezel image where the framebuffer should be composited (in bezel-image pixel units); for round displays it is the bounding square of the circle. `screen_rotation` rotates the framebuffer clockwise (degrees) before compositing. `waveshare_url` is a link to the product page for reference. `driver` is the real Waveshare driver module/class this panel maps to (e.g. 'epd7in3f', 'LCD_1inch28', 'OLED_1in3'), or null when there is no portable vendor driver (IT8951 12.48\"/9.7\"/10.3\", character LCDs); it drives both the vendor-API shim the sandbox exposes and the ready-to-run device snippet. `api` is the fidelity + vendor-API family that selects the exact quantization the panel's controller performs: 'epaper_mono' | 'epaper_4gray' | 'epaper_gray16' | 'epaper_redblack' | 'epaper_4color' | 'epaper_6color' | 'epaper_7color' | 'lcd_rgb565' | 'oled_mono' | 'oled_gray16' | 'oled_rgb' | 'char_hd44780'. The same `api`-driven quantization (see backend/sim/quantize.py) is used by both the simple `waveshare_sim.display` API and the vendor-driver shims, so the browser preview is byte-identical to what the panel would render.",
